# AI-Based Spam Message Detector

This project builds an AI/NLP system to classify SMS messages as "ham" or "spam" using TF-IDF features and baseline machine learning models (Multinomial Naive Bayes and Linear SVM). It includes a CLI for training and prediction plus a notebook for EDA and model comparison.

## Features
- NLP preprocessing with tokenization, stop-word removal, and optional stemming
- Real-time message prediction with confidence scores
- Model comparison (Naive Bayes vs Linear SVM)
- Reproducible training and evaluation pipeline
- Notebook for EDA and reporting

## Project Structure
- `src/spamdetector/` - core package (pipeline, training, CLI)
- `scripts/` - dataset download and preparation
- `data/` - local datasets (not tracked)
- `models/` - saved model artifacts (not tracked)
- `notebooks/` - EDA and modeling notebook
- `reports/` - optional figures/exports

## Setup
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
pip install -e .
```

The editable install adds a `spamdetector` command so you do not need `PYTHONPATH`.

Optional NLTK data (stopwords):
```bash
python -c "import nltk; nltk.download('stopwords')"
```

## Dataset Download and Preparation
This project expects the UCI SMS Spam Collection dataset. The helper script downloads and prepares a CSV at `data/processed/sms.csv`.

```bash
python scripts/download_prepare.py --download --prepare
```

If you already downloaded the dataset manually, place `SMSSpamCollection` under `data/raw/` and run:
```bash
python scripts/download_prepare.py --prepare
```

## Train and Evaluate
Train both models and store the best one in `models/`:
```bash
spamdetector train --data data/processed/sms.csv --model both
```

Evaluate a saved model:
```bash
spamdetector evaluate --data data/processed/sms.csv --model-path models/best_model.joblib
```

## Predict
Predict a single message:
```bash
spamdetector predict --model-path models/best_model.joblib --text "Win a free prize now"
```

Predict a file (one message per line):
```bash
spamdetector predict --model-path models/best_model.joblib --file data/sample_messages.txt
```

## Web Interface
Train a model first so `models/best_model.joblib` exists:
```bash
spamdetector train --data data/processed/sms.csv --model both
```

Run the FastAPI app:
```bash
uvicorn spamdetector.web:app --reload
```

Open http://127.0.0.1:8000 and paste a full email message.

Optional: point to a different model path:
```bash
$env:SPAMDETECTOR_MODEL="models/best_model.joblib"
```

## Notebook
Open the notebook in `notebooks/` to run EDA and compare models. Run the data preparation step first so `data/processed/sms.csv` is available.

## Notes
- The SVM model is calibrated by default to produce probability scores.
- If NLTK stopwords are unavailable, the pipeline falls back to scikit-learn stopwords.

## Future Work
- Hyperparameter tuning and additional features
- Deep learning models (RNN/LSTM)
- UI or API integration
